This file lists the licenses of third-party dependencies of phasm-core,
its companion phasm-cli, and the app/web bridges that embed it (iOS,
Android, WASM). The Rust crate list is the union of the resolved
dependency trees (`cargo tree -e normal,build`) of:

  - ios-bridge / android-bridge (the shipped apps):
    `phasm-core` with `parallel, video, h264-encoder, av1-encoder,
    av1-decoder`, for aarch64-apple-ios / aarch64-linux-android;
  - ios-bridge-decode (App Clip), wasm-bridge and wasm-bridge-decode
    (the website and phasm.link): `parallel` / `wasm`;
  - phasm-cli (`--features parallel,h264-encoder`).

The `h264-encoder` feature additionally pulls in the
`phasm-openh264` C/C++ source via the `core-openh264-sys` workspace
member; that source is BSD-2-Clause licensed and attributed
separately under GROUP 7 below. The `av1-decoder` / `av1-encoder`
features compile the `phasm-dav1d` C source (core-dav1d-sys, GROUP 9)
and the `phasm-rav1e` Rust encoder (GROUP 10). The video codecs back an
experimental feature; they are present in the app binaries, so their
notices belong here.

All listed licenses are compatible with the phasm-core GPL-3.0-only
umbrella. No GPL/AGPL/LGPL transitive dependencies exist (every crate's
`license` field was checked; libfuzzer-sys, NCSA, is an optional rav1e
fuzzing dependency that no build compiles); permissive upstream crates
remain re-distributable under their own terms.

Crates are grouped by license family. Within each family, crates that
require explicit notice retention (BSD, Apache-2.0-only) are spelled
out individually with their copyright lines and full license text;
crates available under permissive multi-licenses where MIT is one of
the choices are summarized.

